@carlfk - @Leo Moser (mole99)'s FPGA is better than the first ever FPGA xilinx released (the xc2064) 🙂 
 * https://spectrum.ieee.org/chip-hall-of-fame-xilinx-xc2064-fpga
 * https://www.righto.com/2020/09/reverse-engineering-first-fpga-chip.html
 * https://github.com/shirriff/xc2064

@digshadow was involved in that work to document that part too.

I always had the dream of having the same (open source) FPGA toolchain be able to produce a bitstream for both Xilinx's modern parts and it's first ever part.
